{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f002","f042"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=hci-completed-length-trust; Search only snapshots/s01. New mechanism branch surfaced by facts f002 and f042, genuinely distinct from the four planned branches (parse-time wire counts, allocation arithmetic, error-unwind poisoned counts, peer-transport reply fields): completion-time transfer metadata — urb->actual_length and analogues such as SCSI/DMA request actual/residual (resid) counts and controller-set completion lengths, written by hardware or device firmware at completion time — consumed by completion handlers as a copy length, subtraction operand, or iteration bound without cross-check against the locally requested size such as transfer_buffer_length or the expected byte count. Known shapes from sibling audits to verify in this tree's exact state if present: drivers/usb/serial/opticon.c:76 'size_t data_len = urb->actual_length - 2;' (size_t underflow when a short or malicious completion reports actual_length < 2), drivers/usb/serial/kl5kusb105.c:360 'len = urb->actual_length - KLSI_HDR_LEN;', and the greybus es2.c bulk-in completion handing urb->actual_length into greybus_data_rcvd/gb_connection_recv whose memcpy destination is sized from local request state. Then sweep the other URB/request completion handlers in this one snapshot that use actual_length/actual/resid/byte_count as copy, loop, or subtraction operands (usb serial/core/misc/media/net/input, scsi resid paths, greybus/serdev, tty receive). Scope strictly to metadata the hardware/controller writes at completion time; parse-time wire counts, allocator arithmetic, and error-path leftover counts are covered by other branch intents on this snapshot and must not be re-reported here. For each candidate record file:line of the completion callback, the metadata field, the missing bound check, and the consuming copy/loop; a negative result must cite the completion handlers examined. The seed usbip path itself is demonstration-only and must never be reported as the finding; if unpatched usbip code is present, record it as excluded-by-rule and keep searching. Save a structured artifact (execution_status, candidates or evidence-backed negative) for snapshots/s01 only."}
